## bodies-in-liquids

bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-ask = Does a bubble’s speed depend on its size?
bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-title = A bubble in a bottle: uniform motion
bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-bench-setup = A clear 0.5 L bottle of thick washing-up liquid with marks, a ruler, a stopwatch
bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-choices = A bigger bubble rises faster
bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-choices-2 = It does not
bodies-in-liquids-bubble-speed-choices-3 = A smaller bubble rises faster
bodies-in-liquids-liquid-label = The liquid in the bottle
bodies-in-liquids-liquid-options = Washing-up liquid
bodies-in-liquids-liquid-options-2 = Glycerol
bodies-in-liquids-build-what = glycerol
bodies-in-liquids-build-what-2 = thick washing-up liquid
bodies-in-liquids-build-question = A clear bottle of { $what } with marks every 3 cm. We turn it over and watch a small air bubble (≈ 2 mm): start the stopwatch as it passes the zero mark and note the time at 3, 6, 9 and 12 cm. Then the same with a bigger bubble (≈ 4 mm). Does a bubble’s speed depend on its size?
bodies-in-liquids-ball-ask = In which liquid does the ball sink slowest?
bodies-in-liquids-ball-title = A ball in liquids of different densities
bodies-in-liquids-ball-choices = In glycerol
bodies-in-liquids-ball-choices-2 = In oil
bodies-in-liquids-ball-choices-3 = In water
bodies-in-liquids-diameter-label = The ball
bodies-in-liquids-diameter-options = 1 mm
bodies-in-liquids-diameter-options-2 = 1.5 mm
bodies-in-liquids-setup = 250 mL measuring cylinders of glycerol, sunflower oil and water, with marks; a steel bearing ball, a stopwatch
bodies-in-liquids-ball-question = Three measuring cylinders: of glycerol (density 1261 kg/m³), sunflower oil (919 kg/m³) and water (997 kg/m³), each with marks every 5 cm. We drop a steel ball { $d } mm across into each: start the stopwatch as it passes the zero mark and note the time at 5, 10 and 15 cm. We find the ball’s speed in each liquid. In which liquid does it sink slowest?
